albedo_color = Color(0.906, 0.925, 0.914, 1)
roughness = 0.55
metallic = 0.0

; Recessed-panel infill — a flat, deliberately darker tone rather than a
; reuse of wall2.tres: in this project's ambient-only lighting (no sky, no
; probes, see MIGRATION_NOTES §Materials) two triplanar materials of similar
; luminance don't separate just because one sits behind the other in Z —
; there's no AO/contact-shadow pass to sell the step. Baking the contrast
; into albedo (like the original's painted outline, but now real geometry
; that still catches a grazing light correctly) is what actually reads.
; m_panel IS GONE. It was a flat StandardMaterial3D — one albedo, one
; roughness, no mottle, no chip, no normal — applied to the two LARGEST
; surfaces on the door. Everything around them ran materials/door.tres, the
; worn triplanar shader, so the door was a detailed frame around two blank
; swatches, and the blank swatches are most of what you look at. That is why
; the door read as "a flat monochrome texture" no matter how much the frame
; was tuned.
;
; The panels now use materials/door.tres like every other painted part. They
; are the same paint as the rails in reality, and the recess is what
; distinguishes them — geometry, not a second material.

